      "math_academy_id": "q-35257",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Let $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=5{b}_{2}$ and ${c}_{2}=-2{b}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}-6{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-6{b}_{2}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5}(5{b}_{2})-\\frac{3}{2}(-2{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{5}{c}_{1}-\\frac{3}{2}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{6}{5} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}].$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
